{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgh5ywZBobXummx4bQSYX", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If BillingService goes down, two services stop working: **RenewalsWorker** and **ReportingService**. I searched up to 4 hops of callers and found nothing else.\n\n**What breaks directly**\n\n| Service | How it's connected | Likely effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| **RenewalsWorker** | DEPENDS_ON \u2192 BillingService | Renewals stop being processed. |\n| **ReportingService** | DEPENDS_ON \u2192 BillingService | Billing-related reports fail or go stale. |\n\nNo other services depend on these two, so the outage doesn't spread any further.\n\n**What doesn't break**\n\nBillingService relies on these, but they keep running while it's down:\n- **PaymentsAPI** and **NotificationsAPI**: BillingService calls them. They'll just stop getting calls from it, so billing-triggered payments and notifications won't happen.\n- **OrderService** and **UserService**: BillingService depends on them. They aren't affected.\n- **BillingPostgresDatabase** and **OrdersPostgresDatabase**: BillingService writes to both. The databases stay up, but no new billing data gets written, which is probably why ReportingService's data would go stale.\n\n**Limits of this answer**\n- The graph only records CALLS and DEPENDS_ON links between services. Anything that reads BillingPostgresDatabase directly, without going through BillingService, wouldn't appear here. It would only see stale data, not an outage.\n- No configuration keys came up, because this question is about service dependencies, not config settings."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 410, "cache_read_input_tokens": 4388, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 410}, "output_tokens": 7, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "1ae5d21f-8348-42fb-a690-bb10c6433c4b", "uuid": "9614363c-e40c-41ae-91b9-8ba515e2e71d", "timestamp": "2026-11-04T02:19:07.546Z", "request_id": "req_011Cgh5ywLYAU8dhthiVUUFg"}
